/T ( The naturally occurring substance kojic acid, which is produced by several fungi including Aspergillus oryzae, has recently gained a lot of interest in the beauty, dermatological, and food preservation industries. The mycelium of Aspergillus oryzae was grown on steamed rice when Saito found KA in 1907. The "koji" in the name of the fungus that produced it is where the term "kojic acid" first appeared. Yabuta gave the chemical the name "kojic acid" in 1913. The leftover residue from fermenting rice for malting is where the Japanese word "koji," meaning steamed rice, comes from. Yabuta also gave a detailed breakdown of kojic acid's chemical  composition.  There after, additional studies)
/E ( The naturally occurring substance kojic acid, which is produced by several fungi including Aspergillus oryzae, has recently gained a lot of interest in the beauty, dermatological, and food preservation industries. The mycelium of Aspergillus oryzae was grown on steamed rice when Saito found KA in 1907. The "koji" in the name of the fungus that produced it is where the term "kojic acid" first appeared. Yabuta gave the chemical the name "kojic acid" in 1913. The leftover residue from fermenting rice for malting is where the Japanese word "koji," meaning steamed rice, comes from. Yabuta also gave a detailed breakdown of kojic acid's chemical  composition.  There after, additional studies)
