/Title (Kojic acid, a metabolite derived from fungi such as Aspergillus oryzae and Penicillium, has garnered substantial interest for its versatile applications in food, cosmetics, and pharmaceuticals due to its skin-whitening, antibacterial, and antioxidant properties. This study explores the utilization of agro-industrial wastes, including sugarcane bagasse, maize steep liquor, and rice bran, as substrates in the efficient fermentation process to produce kojic acid. Employing fungi like Aspergillus oryzae and Aspergillus flavus, researchers achieved significant yields, demonstrating the economic viability of this approach. Kojic acid's wide range of applications includes delaying food browning, enhancing cosmetic formulations, and serving as an antimicrobial agent in medicinal products. It is also noted for its potential in cancer treatment and environmental remediation. Future research aims to optimize production processes, evaluate environmental impacts, and explore genetic modifications to enhance yields. The compound's favorable safety profile and natural origin position it as a promising additive in various industries, particularly as consumer demand for non-toxic and sustainable products rises.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 499 0 R
>>
endobj
