/Title (practice for improving peak sharpness and resolution. The absorbance peak of kojic acid is at 270 nm, thus that's the usual setting for a UV detector used for detection. The concentrations of samples can be measured using a calibration curve that is typically established by first creating standard solutions with kojic acid. This method allows for the precise measurement of kojic acid in different samples, guaranteeing trustworthy outcomes for research and industrial applications alike.)
